			"date": "2025-03-20T14:20:21.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span>  That used to keep me up at night when I worked at Adobe. Back then CoPilot would spit out code verbatim from GPL projects. We didn't want to be the legal test case so the OSPO (engineers/lawyers) recommended strongly we do not use these AI code generators until there is established case law.</p><p>That is for a Fortune 500 level company. As a dev hacking on a side project the risk is not as great. As my Dad would say, “Never sue poor people.”</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
