			},
			"date": "2025-03-21T05:24:41.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.online/@macdonst\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>macdonst</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> this does not look sane at all. Thanks MUCH for the quote.<br>Imagine that this kind of responsibility extends to patent suits or to purpose (two different things)…</p><p>Code is made to be readable so that a human can read and write it and take responsibility. Not doing so is just part of the stupid rush of productivity that managers hope but just makes no sense. </p><p>If code is to be produced faster then you need better (more reliable…) libraries.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
